WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.980
In June 632, the Prophet Muhammad died.

2
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.220
Muslims believe no new
prophet would follow him.

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:12.270
Today, most Muslims are Sunni,
and around 1 in 10 are Shi'a.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.270
Both share one God, one
Qur'an and one Prophet.

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.040
Both honour Ali.

6
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.890
So why did one question,
asked in 632, divide them?

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.190
In this mission, you'll
visit a meeting hall,

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.810
and a desert pool called Ghadir Khumm.

9
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.340
Then you'll compare the
two traditions today,

10
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.880
and weigh up whether the
split was only about politics.

11
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: find out how one question
in 632 divided Sunni and Shi'a Muslims.
